WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates — Week 26 Leader Video
Unit 7, Lesson 2: Falsehood

1
00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:14.970
So 7.2, we call it falsehood and this lesson really is a response to a common atheist objection

2
00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:21.970
that if God was so big and mighty and powerful and sovereign and all good,

3
00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:24.970
then he would have prevented evil.

4
00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:26.970
He wouldn't have allowed it in the first place.

5
00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:30.970
I mean, think about it, if God can do these things, if God can just speak

6
00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:35.970
and suddenly we have a universe, then why can't he prevent evil?

7
00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:41.970
Years ago, I did a debate with an atheist and this was sort of his argument.

8
00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:47.970
His argument was pretty complex, but let me sort of summarize it as quickly as I can.

9
00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:54.970
He basically said that if God existed, God would have created a world

10
00:00:54.970 --> 00:01:00.970
in which only God-like objects existed and he called that God-world.

11
00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:07.970
And if this God-world were an actual world, then all the pieces of God-world would be just like God.

12
00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:10.970
There would be no suffering, there would be no evil, there would be no nothing.

13
00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:16.970
Everything would be absolutely perfect on equal playing field to God.

14
00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:18.970
And my response was pretty simple.

15
00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:23.970
It took me some time to figure out exactly what he was saying and then it hit me.

16
00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:28.970
I said, well, one, why do you think this is the case?

17
00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:31.970
And he said, well, because there's evil and suffering in the world.

18
00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:33.970
I said, well, let's put that aside for a second.

19
00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:37.970
Is there anything that God cannot do?

20
00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:41.970
And he said, well, if God is all-powerful, then there's nothing that God cannot do.

21
00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:47.970
That's why if he can't prevent evil, then God must not exist.

22
00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:49.970
I said, that's not the case.

23
00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:57.970
Just because God is all-powerful and sovereign and omniscient and all-awesome,

24
00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:02.970
then does that mean that there's nothing that God cannot do?

25
00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.970
So unfortunately, the old song, my God is so great, my God is so big,

26
00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:08.970
there's nothing that's actually not necessarily true.

27
00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:16.970
Because God could not create a world in which only God-like objects or God-like things,

28
00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.970
that are equivalent to him, existed.

29
00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:24.970
Because if that were the case, then God would not exist,

30
00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:28.970
because he wouldn't be God anymore.

31
00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:32.970
He would just be equal to everything else, then everything would be the same as God

32
00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:39.970
and all things would be God, and that would take us into a form of pantheism.

33
00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:42.970
So his argument didn't work.

34
00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:45.970
But it's sort of this understanding that, well, why wouldn't God do that?

35
00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:50.970
Well, because simply put, there's some things that God actually cannot do.

36
00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.970
And what's important about this lesson is to help students understand that

37
00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:56.970
God is not the one that's responsible for evil.

38
00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:57.970
God did not create it.

39
00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:01.970
It's like I've said last week, it's not a thing to be created because evil is not a thing.

40
00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:04.970
God did not create it. God is not responsible.

41
00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:10.970
And although God is doing something to remedy the situation,

42
00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:14.970
he still has to allow us to have free will to make our own choices.

43
00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:19.970
So this week, I would get your students thinking about the character and nature of who God is.

44
00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.970
Have them think about, just like in the intro activity,

45
00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.970
we ask them about things that it's impossible for humanity to do,

46
00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:28.970
but what about things that are impossible for God to do?

47
00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:31.970
What are some other things that maybe God cannot do?

48
00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:36.970
Have your students sort of think that through of what makes God God

49
00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:40.970
and what maybe limits does God actually have?

50
00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:44.970
Now I don't mean fun things like can God create a rock so big

51
00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:46.970
he can't lift it in those strange questions like that.

52
00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:48.970
That's not what I'm talking about.

53
00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:51.970
But things like God cannot contradict himself.

54
00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:53.970
God cannot lie.

55
00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:58.970
So have your students think that through to help paint a better picture

56
00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:03.970
of the nature of God and exactly what he's doing in this world

57
00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:07.970
to remedy the evil and the suffering that is so prevalent.

58
00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:13.970
So God has morally justified reasons for allowing the temporary existence

59
00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:16.970
of evil and suffering in our world.

60
00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:19.970
That may seem like a cop out, like what?

61
00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:22.970
That's the best you've got.

62
00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:25.970
But remember what Scripture says and what Paul says in 1 Corinthians

63
00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:29.970
is that we only see things in part right now.

64
00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:31.970
We don't have a full picture.

65
00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:33.970
There's still quite a bit of mystery going on.

66
00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:37.970
The example I always used to give my students was

67
00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:40.970
the example of being a kid or parenting my own kids

68
00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:43.970
is that I may know what's best for my kids.

69
00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:45.970
They may not realize that I know what's best

70
00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:47.970
and what I'm telling them they have to do

71
00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:49.970
or what I'm putting them through

72
00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:52.970
may seem like a terrible, terrible thing for them in that moment.

73
00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:55.970
The whole world is coming crashing down on them

74
00:04:55.970 --> 00:04:58.970
yet I know exactly what I'm doing and it's for their good.

75
00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:00.970
And that may be the case sometimes

76
00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:04.970
and sometimes it's just the case that evil is just evil

77
00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:06.970
and evil just happens.

78
00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:10.970
And God doesn't like it any more than we do

79
00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:14.970
but he has to allow it even if only for a time.

80
00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:16.970
And as we'll see later on

81
00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:18.970
when we get to more of the pastoral approach

82
00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:20.970
to this question of evil

83
00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:25.970
is that it can be used for something exceptionally good.

84
00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.970
So in your small groups

85
00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:29.970
I want you to start to brainstorm a little bit

86
00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.970
about what good can come from evil.

87
00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:34.970
But I also want you to again be very aware

88
00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:36.970
when I keep beating this drum

89
00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:38.970
be very aware of the questions that are coming.

90
00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:40.970
If the questions didn't come last week

91
00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:42.970
they may be coming this week

92
00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:44.970
and they may be coming next week

93
00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:46.970
they may be coming all of the weeks.

94
00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:48.970
And be aware of some of the things

95
00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:50.970
that your students are going through.

96
00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:52.970
By now you probably know your students really well

97
00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:54.970
you probably know their families

98
00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:57.970
you probably have talked with their parents

99
00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:00.970
and you've connected with their families on some level.

100
00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:03.970
Do your best to be aware of some of the things

101
00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:05.970
that your students are going through

102
00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:06.970
for two reasons.

103
00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:08.970
One so you can pray with them

104
00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:10.970
and pastor them along and walk with them

105
00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:14.970
and be there for them in the way that you need to be.

106
00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:16.970
That goes without saying.

107
00:06:16.970 --> 00:06:19.970
But the other is when we're dealing with these kinds of issues

108
00:06:19.970 --> 00:06:22.970
you want to have an awareness and a sensitivity

109
00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:24.970
so that you don't say anything

110
00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:26.970
that would touch the wrong nerve

111
00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:27.970
with your students.

112
00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:29.970
Sometimes you may want to a little bit

113
00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:31.970
to get a response out of students

114
00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:32.970
and to move them along

115
00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:35.970
but you also want to be very very very aware

116
00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:36.970
of where they are

117
00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:38.970
so that you can minister to them

118
00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:40.970
the best possible way

119
00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:42.970
without saying them back at all.

120
00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:45.970
So rather than going down the easy road

121
00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:47.970
and just simply doubting God

122
00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:50.970
because of the evil that we see around us

123
00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:53.970
we can actually look to him for hope

124
00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:55.970
and know that he has a plan

125
00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:57.970
know that he has a purpose

126
00:06:57.970 --> 00:07:00.970
and know that of all the things that we're going through

127
00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:02.970
it's not for nothing.

128
00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:06.970
We can look to him for significant hope.

